<archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate"
    name="ADR-001 MOP database access route"
    id="id-eeaefefea96c45348c25e1520091f4ee"
    documentation="MOP database access route for the Orchestration pattern.&#xA;The pilot proves Orchestration with a read-only MOP API, hosted on AKS and exposed to consumers through API Management, with Entra ID OAuth 2.0 security.&#xA;The API is built against a development copy of the MOP Oracle database on an Azure VM, and cannot go beyond development until it has a suitable data source.&#xA;The on-premise database sits on Windows Server 2008 R2 behind an end-of-life firewall and is linked to PCS, L&amp;C and TMS, so the route must add no risk to them.&#xA;Azure Relay was rejected; a permanent fix (migrate or decouple) is outside the pilot timeframe.&#xA;Preferred for the pilot: Option 2, a snapshot copied to Azure as a temporary, read-only source. Status: Proposed, decision pending.">
